WEBVTT

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:07.190
It's so cute.

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:11.720
Gramps says you can name this one.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:12.650
Really?

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:14.540
Let's see...

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:16.120
I like "Choko."

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.380
Because it goes <i>chokochoko</i> 
tottering around.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.290
That sounds good.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.120
You're going to have to give it 
lots of love.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:25.260
Yup.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:50.360
There.

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:54.680
Thanks as always, Fuuka-chan.

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:56.330
It's delicious.

00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:58.170
Shall I make some tea?

00:00:58.170 --> 00:00:59.580
I'll have some.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:07.660
I know you're freeloading, 
but you don't have to do all this for us.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:11.210
It makes me happy 
to see you appreciate it, though.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:13.510
If you say so, Fuuka.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.710
Thanks.

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:18.110
Oh, I have remedial classes today.

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:19.450
I'll see you at work.

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:20.620
Got it.

00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:32.980
You can leave once you've
submitted your work.

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:35.040
Later, Sensei.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:35.760
Yep.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:37.050
You'd better be here tomorrow.

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:37.880
Sure.

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:39.340
Bye, Sensei.

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:41.360
Misakino.

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:41.990
Yeah?

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:44.750
Your brain's an aquarium, isn't it?

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:46.170
It is.

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:50.940
That's fine and all, 
but you need to stop missing classes,

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:53.150
or you're going to have 
a hard time graduating.

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:57.130
I wouldn't mind quitting, 
but Gramps says I should finish high school.

00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:58.920
Listen...

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:03.660
I've been going easy on you, because I know 
you're going to inherit the aquarium.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:05.580
But it might be closing, right?

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.480
Who told you that?!

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.400
It's just a rumor.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:12.020
I heard you're the director there right now.

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:14.320
You're a high-schooler.

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:15.690
You need to take it easy.

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:19.990
No one's going to do it if I don't!

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:22.730
Pardon me.

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:30.860
It's a gift to have something 
you care about so much, but I mean...

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:35.670
Misakino-san.

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:37.600
Are you going to the aquarium again?

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:38.320
Yeah.

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:39.840
I'm on my way there.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:41.740
You're so hard working. 
Good for you.

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:42.970
I support you.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:45.900
You could come hang out, 
if you want to support me.

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:48.560
We're going to hold a bunch
of events over the summer.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:50.090
Okay.

00:02:50.090 --> 00:02:51.710
I'll go on a date there.

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:52.230
Huh?

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:53.770
You have a boyfriend?

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:56.220
I'll make sure I have one 
by the end of this summer.

00:02:57.330 --> 00:02:58.570
See you.

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:00.360
Bye.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:09.990
Kuuya-kun, I'm done for the day.

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:12.380
You're leaving already?

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:13.020
Yeah.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:14.800
I'm headed to Fukuoka.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.590
I'll be late.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:20.240
Any luck finding people to adopt the animals?

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:22.840
For only about half of them.

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:24.360
I see.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:25.500
Don't worry.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:28.470
I'll find people to adopt the staff, too.

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:34.190
No, I was kind of taken in by you.

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:37.660
I haven't really thought about the future.

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:49.800
Thank you.

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:00.260
This is so cute.

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:02.010
<b>First Penguin</b>

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:02.010
<b>Key chains</b>

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:04.320
"First Penguin"?

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:05.790
Oh, those?

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:07.760
The acting director made those.

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:09.890
They don't sell too well.

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:13.680
The postcards sell out.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:15.760
Be sure to stock extra.

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:17.180
Got it.

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:18.400
Nope. Nope.

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:26.660
<b>What's a First Penguin?</b>

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:26.660
<b>Someone who courageously takes on risks, 
like the first penguin that jumps into the water regardless of circumstances. 
It can terrifying to be the first person to challenge something new, 
but once you do, the others will follow. A First Penguin has strength 
within them to have a positive impact on the people around them.</b>

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:26.660
<i>"Someone who courageously takes on risks,</i>

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:31.700
<i>like the first penguin that jumps 
into the water regardless of circumstances."</i>

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:34.590
It's been a while.

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:35.920
Kai!

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:37.420
Thanks for waiting.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:40.300
I'm here, as promised.

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:44.630
Man, I'm so glad you're a dude.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:46.950
Thanks, Kai-kun.

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:47.480
I've never seen him smile like that.

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:49.690
He's just not good around girls.

00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:51.770
He doesn't mean anything by it.

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:54.260
I'm Nakamura Kai.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.740
I'm going to be working with
you here starting today.

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:56.980
I look forward to it.

00:04:57.640 --> 00:05:00.320
Kai, you can help Kuuya-san with his jobs.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:03.070
Fuuka and I are going to weigh the penguins.

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:04.660
O-Okay.

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:11.380
Penguins...

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:19.040
We weigh each of the penguins, one by one.

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:20.920
I usually start with Choko.

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:28.390
We normally do routine checkups, but the vet, 
Takeshita-sensei, is on maternity leave.

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:30.680
Um, Kukuru...

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:31.900
Director Kukuru.

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:34.200
You can call me "Kukuru," remember?

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:37.600
But it's easier to call you "Director" at work.

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:39.350
Yeah?

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:42.680
How do you tell these kids apart?

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:45.470
You can read the tags on their flippers.

00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:48.170
But you'll start noticing things 
that are unique about each of them.

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:51.850
Choko is friendly and wants to be pampered.

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:53.840
Choko's been here for nearly fifteen years 

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:55.700
and is used to the staff, too.

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:58.580
Oh yeah, when I was feeding them
 the first time...

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:04.800
Choko-san was at the front.

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:08.380
I'm going to be calm this time.

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:14.320
You managed to feed 'em.

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:16.400
Thank goodness.

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:18.430
Choko's a big eater.

00:06:18.430 --> 00:06:19.900
Really?

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:20.830
Yeah.

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:23.640
The attendants have to be able 
to know really quickly

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:27.950
how much they've had to eat 
and adjust their feed.

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:33.550
More for the lighter ones; 
less for the chubby ones, for example.

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:35.450
That's why we weigh them.

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:36.630
Okay.

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:40.870
Eat well, Choko-san.

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:43.180
Huh?

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:45.290
Something seems off.

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:46.520
Choko?

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:47.990
Really?

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:51.680
This is...

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:53.660
Bumblefoot?

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:58.230
<b>June 25, 2006 (Sunday)</b>

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:58.230
<b>Madeleine (Male, 9 years)</b>

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:58.230
<b>Left foot: center sore 
(3.0mm high, 2.9mm wide)</b>

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:58.230
<b>Right foot: center sore 
(4.2mm high, 3.8mm wide)</b>

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:58.230
<b>Area around sores and heels are rough</b>

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:56.510
It's a problem that penguins often have.

00:06:56.510 --> 00:07:00.800
It's kind of like having corns,
but when it gets bad, it can become contagious.

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:02.270
We can't leave it untreated.

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:06.610
Penguins in aquariums tend 
not to get enough activity on their own.

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:09.450
So they're susceptible to these symptoms.

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:12.110
We walk them to try to prevent it.

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:15.990
Just talk to the director when he gets back.

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:19.500
This might be too urgent for that.

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:22.890
Nah, you should leave this to a veteran.

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:25.830
I'm the director!

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:28.650
I'll talk to Takeshita-sensei.

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:30.420
The one on maternity leave?

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:31.550
No, man.

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:33.640
You gotta report to the director first.

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:35.480
I'm just going to make a quick call.

00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:44.170
Really?

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:45.020
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:46.600
<i>I'll go take a quick look.</i>

00:07:46.600 --> 00:07:47.940
<i>You want it checked out quickly, right?</i>

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:49.520
Thank you.

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:50.730
I appreciate it.

00:07:50.730 --> 00:07:51.500
Yes.

00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:52.450
Yes.

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:57.070
Hi, pardon me.

00:07:57.070 --> 00:08:00.580
The director asked me to help you out.

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:03.840
Then, I haven't done these
ones yet, so could you?

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:04.900
Okay.

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:15.300
I'll get it.

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:20.770
Thank you.

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.830
You're like a man of the sea.

00:08:24.550 --> 00:08:25.550
Me?

00:08:25.550 --> 00:08:28.520
You're not really like Kuuya-san.

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:31.240
That guy? For sure.

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:37.180
How are things?

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:39.080
What things?

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:40.520
Kukuru.

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:42.060
You're living with her, aren't you?

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:42.860
Yes.

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:44.580
I'm in her care.

00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:48.390
She can be kind of odd.

00:08:48.390 --> 00:08:52.410
And she's an aquarium freak, 
so she's constantly talking about fish.

00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:53.550
I know what you mean.

00:08:55.350 --> 00:08:59.200
Kukuru lost her parents when she was little.

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:05.480
She used to come to Gama Gama Aquarium 
with her parents a lot, apparently.

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:08.340
Her most precious memories must be here.

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:14.560
Her gramps took her in, 
and she's been helping at the aquarium.

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:19.180
The fish must be 
like a surrogate family to her.

00:09:20.180 --> 00:09:23.830
Her whole reason for becoming the director 
for the summer was to protect this place.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:27.430
I think she's having it rough, 
doing it all by herself.

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:33.770
So I want you to help her out.

00:09:34.280 --> 00:09:36.470
I'll do the best I can, too.

00:09:36.940 --> 00:09:38.620
With heavy lifting and stuff.

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:39.580
Okay.

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:41.980
You're kind, huh?

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:44.190
No, she's just an annoying friend.

00:09:44.190 --> 00:09:45.600
That's all.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:48.350
<b>Kamee Diner</b>

00:09:46.030 --> 00:09:48.350
I'm so pissed!

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:52.570
I keep asking for extensions 
on the subsidies for Gama Gama,

00:09:52.570 --> 00:09:54.990
but they just won't listen.

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:57.740
That's bureaucracy for you.

00:09:57.740 --> 00:10:00.090
Those assholes even had the nerve to tell me

00:10:00.090 --> 00:10:02.490
that it's ridiculous 
the director is a high-schooler.

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:05.350
Hey, watch your language.

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:09.100
I like that you're doing all that for her, though.

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:11.480
You're such a nice person, Karin-chan.

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:20.910
I just don't want to see Gama Gama go away.

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:23.470
I've gone there a ton of times 
since I was little.

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:25.020
It's a precious part of my hometown.

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:27.850
I don't know how to describe it.

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:29.650
I kind of get it.

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:32.910
Besides, how could you not want to support her?

00:10:32.910 --> 00:10:35.230
She's working so hard.

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:40.570
And here's a freebie 
for <i>this</i> hard-working lady.

00:10:41.380 --> 00:10:43.660
Udon-chan!

00:10:47.260 --> 00:10:48.870
Takeshita-sensei!

00:10:49.640 --> 00:10:51.840
Sorry I'm late.

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:54.320
The traffic was really bad.

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:57.270
You've gotten big.

00:10:57.270 --> 00:11:01.800
I'm past due, 
but he just won't come out.

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:03.450
I'm sorry, Sensei.

00:11:03.450 --> 00:11:05.290
I dragged you out here.

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:06.180
It's fine.

00:11:06.490 --> 00:11:10.360
My doctor even told me 
some exercise will do us good.

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:16.250
You're right, Kukuru-chan.

00:11:16.250 --> 00:11:18.070
It's an early case of bumblefoot.

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:19.530
It is, huh?

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:22.360
Let's use wound dressing.

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:25.500
We'll protect the affected area, 
so it doesn't get dirty or wet,

00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:28.940
and observe Choko in a dry area.

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:32.060
That's the best we can do for now.

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:33.580
Understood.

00:11:37.890 --> 00:11:43.040
Sensei, if it's all right, would you be able 
to check on the other penguins?

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:44.760
Sure.

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:47.070
Since I'm here, 
I might as well take a look.

00:11:47.070 --> 00:11:49.020
Thank you!

00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:52.390
But are you really sure?

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:54.380
I'm fine.

00:11:59.480 --> 00:12:01.320
What's wrong?

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:03.640
It hurts a little.

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:13.000
<b>Life Begins In the Ocean</b>

00:12:13.340 --> 00:12:15.500
Are you all right, Sensei?

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:18.750
I think my water broke.

00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:20.760
What do we do?

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:22.380
This is my fault.

00:12:23.170 --> 00:12:24.630
I'm sorry.

00:12:24.630 --> 00:12:26.800
Could you call a taxi?

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:28.700
And get my bag.

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:30.200
O-Okay.

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:36.350
Hey, no running in the aquarium.

00:12:36.350 --> 00:12:37.480
It's about to be born!

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:38.840
The damselfish?

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:39.480
The bag!

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:41.860
Takeshita-sensei's bag!

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:44.240
What's gotten into you, Acting Director?

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:52.200
<i>I have to get a grip.</i>

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:55.230
Kuuya-san, get Kai and Fuuka.

00:12:55.230 --> 00:12:57.580
Takeshita-sensei's water broke.

00:12:57.580 --> 00:12:58.860
Sure.

00:12:59.820 --> 00:13:00.630
Huh?

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:11.420
Are you all right, Sensei?

00:13:11.420 --> 00:13:13.610
I'll leave your bag here.

00:13:13.610 --> 00:13:14.890
Thanks.

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:17.450
I brought towels.

00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:18.440
Thanks.

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:22.590
Does the aquarium not have a car?

00:13:22.590 --> 00:13:25.020
We do, but I don't have a license.

00:13:25.020 --> 00:13:26.780
I'll go look for a taxi.

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:35.580
Excuse us. We need
to use this area for a while.

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:42.840
Hello? It's Takeshita.

00:13:43.330 --> 00:13:45.880
My water broke while I was out.

00:13:46.740 --> 00:13:49.900
Kai, could you put out 
an emergency closing sign outside?

00:13:49.900 --> 00:13:53.370
Give the leaving guests some
postcards to take home.

00:13:53.370 --> 00:13:54.340
All right.

00:13:58.270 --> 00:14:00.060
Hang in there, Sensei.

00:14:00.820 --> 00:14:05.400
I'm sorry. I didn't think
it would come to this.

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:09.360
Sensei, remember what
you told me a long time ago?

00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:13.620
The aquarium is a place 
where we take care of life.

00:14:14.520 --> 00:14:20.010
Always keep in mind that you're in charge 
of the precious lives of other beings.

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:22.680
<i>Protect them with all you've got.</i>

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:28.460
The aquarium takes care 
not just of the lives of fish,

00:14:28.460 --> 00:14:31.580
but of the guests and staff, too.

00:14:32.410 --> 00:14:36.270
So we're going to protect you 
with all we've got.

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:41.220
A place where we take care of life...

00:14:53.820 --> 00:14:55.370
All the taxis are out.

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:57.160
They won't be back for another hour.

00:15:59.180 --> 00:16:00.650
Where's the car?

00:16:08.920 --> 00:16:10.390
We have a car!

00:16:11.290 --> 00:16:12.320
Hello.

00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:14.200
Um...

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:16.120
We couldn't find a taxi.

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:17.920
So we asked a friend for help.

00:16:17.920 --> 00:16:19.920
You could be a bit more appreciative.

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:22.460
Work is busy at the Tourism Association.

00:16:23.760 --> 00:16:25.850
Where should I take you?

00:16:25.850 --> 00:16:27.880
Have you heard of Uchima Maternity Home?

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:29.340
I have.

00:16:29.600 --> 00:16:31.150
I'll come, too.

00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:34.120
No, I'll accompany her.

00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:36.140
You should stay here, Director.

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:37.100
But...

00:16:37.400 --> 00:16:39.600
Give Choko-chan some attention.

00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:43.190
Sorry.

00:16:44.280 --> 00:16:45.740
Please go in my place.

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:51.340
That was stressful.

00:16:51.340 --> 00:16:53.240
Seriously, that scared me.

00:17:00.980 --> 00:17:03.160
Another closure?

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:06.640
They found an unexploded ordnance nearby.

00:17:06.640 --> 00:17:08.090
Don't worry, though.

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:14.780
Now's my chance to show off 
my Tourism Association skills.

00:17:14.780 --> 00:17:16.840
I'm driving around all the time.

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:18.140
A detour isn't going to slow me down.

00:17:21.390 --> 00:17:24.720
Please drive as slowly as you can, 
so it doesn't shake.

00:17:24.720 --> 00:17:26.520
But also, hurry!

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:28.060
That's a tall order.

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:41.030
Is something wrong?

00:17:41.530 --> 00:17:45.540
I just noticed Choko hasn't
been eating as much lately.

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:49.170
Choko's getting old, 
so it's to be expected, but...

00:17:49.550 --> 00:17:51.540
You've got so much to worry about.

00:17:52.110 --> 00:17:54.550
That's the nature of the job.

00:17:54.890 --> 00:17:56.970
Get well soon.

00:18:00.080 --> 00:18:02.680
I hope the doctor's okay.

00:18:04.640 --> 00:18:06.740
Would you like some water?

00:18:06.740 --> 00:18:08.280
No, thanks.

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:12.470
Sorry, my husband should be coming soon.

00:18:17.800 --> 00:18:21.620
I had a strange dream 
at the aquarium earlier.

00:18:23.300 --> 00:18:25.850
It was as if I were in the water.

00:18:25.850 --> 00:18:28.230
The fish came right up to me.

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:32.840
And I met my baby.

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:38.660
He said, "I get to meet you soon, Mom."

00:18:40.440 --> 00:18:42.230
I have to be strong.

00:18:45.330 --> 00:18:47.480
Shall we move you now?

00:18:52.230 --> 00:18:55.110
Do what's right,
and everything will work out.

00:18:56.160 --> 00:18:58.990
Why didn't you contact me?

00:18:58.990 --> 00:19:03.270
You could have talked to me.

00:19:03.270 --> 00:19:07.040
You wouldn't have had 
to trouble the doctor.

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:07.870
But...

00:19:07.870 --> 00:19:09.870
No "buts."

00:19:09.870 --> 00:19:14.300
You can't try to do everything yourself 
just because you're the director.

00:19:14.300 --> 00:19:15.750
I'm sorry.

00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:21.380
Hello?!

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:23.850
Yeah.

00:19:24.420 --> 00:19:25.190
Yeah.

00:19:25.910 --> 00:19:26.720
Yeah.

00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:28.640
She just gave birth.

00:19:29.440 --> 00:19:31.900
Child and mother are doing well.

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:33.960
That's great!

00:19:33.960 --> 00:19:36.250
I was so worried.

00:19:43.430 --> 00:19:45.280
So cute!

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:46.870
Is he asleep?

00:19:47.280 --> 00:19:49.290
He can't open his eyes yet.

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:51.080
I see.

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:54.040
Sensei, I'm really sorry.

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:56.790
Gramps scolded me about it, too.

00:19:57.280 --> 00:19:59.420
No, it's all right.

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:05.590
Thanks to you and Fuuka-chan, 
I'll never forget this birth.

00:20:13.570 --> 00:20:15.060
So cute.

00:20:15.760 --> 00:20:18.100
Mothers are amazing, huh?

00:20:19.220 --> 00:20:20.600
Yeah...

00:20:20.600 --> 00:20:22.030
You might be right.

00:20:23.010 --> 00:20:28.220
But maybe it was this baby who
did the best work by being born healthy.

00:20:28.220 --> 00:20:29.580
Thank you.

00:20:42.970 --> 00:20:47.470
<b>So when ever are you coming home?</b>

00:20:42.970 --> 00:20:47.470
<b>Hey! Answer me!</b>

00:20:42.970 --> 00:20:47.470
<b>Sorry for worrying you, Mom.</b>

00:20:42.970 --> 00:20:47.470
<b>I'm in the care of a place 
called Gama Gama Aquarium for the summer.</b>

00:20:50.340 --> 00:20:51.980
Sensei, hey...

00:20:52.380 --> 00:20:53.530
Yes?

00:20:53.530 --> 00:20:56.540
Where do you get a maternity handbook?

00:20:57.670 --> 00:20:58.730
Are you pregnant?

00:20:58.730 --> 00:21:00.480
O-Of course not!

00:21:02.710 --> 00:21:07.300
You can get one from the municipality 
when you find out that you're pregnant.

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:08.970
Huh.

00:21:11.540 --> 00:21:13.960
<b>Maternity Handbook</b>

00:21:11.540 --> 00:21:13.960
<b>Misakino Kukuru</b>

00:21:23.760 --> 00:21:25.220
Isn't that...

00:21:26.560 --> 00:21:28.510
Oh, er...

00:21:29.130 --> 00:21:31.370
I guess I'm just helping with sales.

00:21:31.370 --> 00:21:33.740
Actually, I just really like it.

00:21:34.630 --> 00:21:40.270
Someday, I want to have the courage 
to challenge myself to something new.

00:21:40.950 --> 00:21:43.400
I made those with that in mind.

00:21:44.850 --> 00:21:47.000
I'm glad you like it, Fuuka!

00:21:48.350 --> 00:21:49.840
We gotta get back to Gama Gama.

00:21:49.840 --> 00:21:51.660
Lunch break's going to be over!

00:21:55.330 --> 00:21:56.480
Hey...

00:21:56.480 --> 00:21:57.500
Yeah?

00:21:58.550 --> 00:22:02.440
Having courage isn't the same 
as being reckless, right?

00:22:02.440 --> 00:22:03.250
Eh?
